 # Registry Specifications
 
-- [ ] **REG-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize surrounding whitespace and ASCII letter case before returning a matching record or NotFound.
-- [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
-- [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
-- [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+## Lookup Behavior
+
+- [ ] **REG-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize the input by stripping leading and trailing whitespace and uppercasing ASCII letters (a–z → A–Z) before querying the index.
+- [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL return the result (Found or NotFound) including the active snapshot's date; the snapshot date is the same regardless of whether a matching record exists.
+- [ ] **REG-003**: When a lookup is performed on a kiosk with an active SQLite index database, the system SHALL complete the lookup in 250 ms or less (P99 latency on target hardware with 90,000 records).
+
+## Snapshot Import & Index Preparation
+
+- [ ] **REG-004**: When a snapshot import is initiated, the system SHALL validate the signature using the bundled public key; if the signature is invalid, the system SHALL reject the import with a signature verification error and retain the active snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When a snapshot import is initiated and the signature is valid, the system SHALL validate that all records have unique serial numbers; if duplicates exist, the system SHALL reject the import with a duplicate serial number error and retain the active snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When a snapshot import is initiated and the signature is valid and serial numbers are unique, the system SHALL reject the import if the schema version is unsupported, report the unsupported version, and retain the active snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When all validation phases pass during snapshot import, the system SHALL create a temporary SQLite database with an indexed table of records and build a B-tree index on the normalized serial column.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: When snapshot index preparation completes successfully, the system SHALL atomically replace the active snapshot database, ensuring the previous snapshot remains available until the new one is fully readable.
+- [ ] **REG-009**: When snapshot import fails at any phase, the system SHALL report the specific error encountered and ensure the previous snapshot database remains active and available for lookups.
+
+## Snapshot Date and Metadata
+
+- [ ] **REG-010**: The system SHALL store the snapshot import date in the active SQLite database and expose this date in all lookup results.
